{{Quote|Would I be out here in the cold if I had just pinched 100 million credits?|Saw Gerrera, to Luthen Rael|<ref name="Narkina 5" />}}
'''Segra Milo''', or '''Segra-Milo''', was a barren [[planet]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Jospro sector]]. Originally the site of [[Mining|mines]], the world became abandoned before the [[Partisans]] rebel cell used a mine there as a [[starfighter]] [[Saw Gerrera's Base|launch base]]. Their operations prompted increased patrols by the [[Galactic Empire]] in the area, with Segra Milo falling under a labeled [[Pirate|piracy]] zone. The rebel agent [[Luthen Rael]] met with Partisans leader [[Saw Gerrera]] there multiple times in [[5 BBY]], initially offering stolen technology in return for assisting in a [[Spellhaus attack|tactical strike]] against the Empire before turning back on the offer when the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] caught wind of the attack plans.

On his way out from Segra Milo the latter time, Rael encountered an [[Segra-Milo Imperial patrol|Imperial patrol]], which attempted to pull his [[Luthen Rael's Fondor Haulcraft|Fondor Haulcraft]] in by [[tractor beam]]. Initially stalling the Imperials, the agent broke the peace by damaging the tractor beam and destroying the subsequently deployed [[Segra-Milo Imperial patrol's air wing|air wing]] before escaping into [[hyperspace]].

==Description==
[[File:Benthic_Segra_Milo.png|thumb|left|300px|The Partisan launch base on Segra Milo]]
Segra Milo,<ref name="Narkina 5" /> or similarly written as Segra-Milo,<ref name="Captain Elk">{{Databank|captain-elk|Captain Elk}}</ref> was a terrestrial [[planet]] located in a [[star system]] of the [[Segra Milo system|same name]], within an intersecting portion of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Guide" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> Part of the [[Jospro sector]],<ref name="Guide" /> it fell within grid square R-7 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="CLNE" /> The world was 10,318 [[kilometer]]s, or 6,411 miles, in diameter and had a single [[moon]].<ref name="Guide" /> Appearing green and brown [[color]]ed from above,<ref name="Narkina 5" /> Segra Milo was barren<ref name="Guide" /> and included rugged valleys,<ref name="Narkina 5" /> rocky expanses, and cliffs and [[mountain]]s,<ref name="Guide" /> including a network of [[cave]]rns.<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> The planet had a Type I [[atmosphere]]<ref name="Atmosphere" /> breathable to [[human]]s and other [[species]], and the climate was [[Temperature|cold]] and sometimes [[cloud]]y,<ref name="Narkina 5" /> considered miserable by some.<ref name="Guide" />

==History==
===Partisan activity===
{{Quote|Is there something wrong, patrol?''"<br />"''There's been partisan activity in the area. This is a piracy zone.|Luthen Rael and Captain Elk|<ref name="Daughter">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref>}}
By the [[Imperial Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], Segra Milo hosted [[Mining|mines]] that were eventually exhausted, the world being abandoned afterward. During the Empire's reign, the [[Partisans]], a group of extremist rebels led by the revolutionary [[Saw Gerrera]], used a mine on the planet as a [[starfighter]] [[Saw Gerrera's Base|launch base]]<ref name="Guide" /> by [[5 BBY]].<ref name="5 BBY">{{AndorDate|108}}</ref> Due to the Partisan activity,<ref name="Daughter" /> a trade outpost in a neighboring [[sector]] began complaining about [[pirate]] activity, prompting an increase in Imperial patrols near Segra Milo,<ref name="Guide" /> which they labeled as part of a piracy zone.<ref name="Daughter" /> The patrols made Gerrera begin considering relocating the base, which would have been a costly move for him.<ref name="Guide" />

[[File:Luthen-Saw-Andor8.png|thumb|right|300px|Luthen Rael speaks with Saw Gerrera at the Partisan base.]]
In 5 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]],<ref name="5 BBY" /> [[Luthen Rael]], a rebel agent that coordinated a shadowy [[Axis network|network]] between different rebel cells, traveled to Segra Milo on his [[Luthen Rael's Fondor Haulcraft|Fondor Haulcraft]] to meet with Gerrera. Landing at the Partisan launch base, Rael spoke with Gerrera and offered stolen Imperial technology in exchange for the Partisans helping a [[Anto Kreegyr's group|rebel cell]] led by [[Neo-Separatist Coalition|Neo-Separatist]] [[Anto Kreegyr]] in [[Spellhaus attack|attacking]] the [[Spellhaus Imperial power station|Imperial power station]]<ref name="Narkina 5" /> on the astronomical object<ref name="Guide" /> [[Spellhaus]]. Gerrera refused to work with Kreegyr, calling the other rebel group lost. Rael departed without his intended deal.<ref name="Narkina 5" />

Later on, Gerrera had a change in heart and decided he wanted in on Kreegyr's attack, making research on Spellhaus and calling over Rael. When Rael arrived and heard Gerrera's news, he stopped the Partisan leader's plans and revealed that the Empire's [[Imperial Security Bureau]] (ISB) already knew of Kreegyr's attack. Confused, Gerrera grew distrustful of the rebel agent, believing that he thought the rebel cells were expendable. Although the confrontation briefly got heated, Rael was able to reassure his associate and convince him that letting Kreegyr's group walk into a trap would give the ISB a false sense of security and allow the rebels to play the long game. Gerrera agreed with Rael, who departed shortly thereafter.<ref name="Daughter" />

===Patrol encounter===
{{Quote|This is Segra-Milo Imperial patrol. Please identify yourself, Haulcraft.''"<br />"''Sorry, can you repeat back please?''"<br />"''This is an Imperial patrol. Standby for transponder scan.|Captain Elk and Luthen Rael|audio=Elk-Rael-Patrol.flac|<ref name="Daughter" />}}
[[File:HaulcraftArrestor-DaughterofFerrix.png|thumb|left|300px|An Imperial patrol stops Rael's Fondor Haulcraft above Segra Milo.]]
Above Segra Milo, Rael made contact with his colleague [[Kleya Marki]], who spoke in codewords with him about an opportunity to catch up with one of his rogue agents, [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]]. The conversation was cut short when an [[Segra-Milo Imperial patrol|Imperial patrol]], comprising a [[Elk's Cantwell-class Arrestor Cruiser|''Cantwell''-class Arrestor Cruiser]] [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by [[Captain]] [[Elk]], arrived and [[Jammer|jammed]] communications. Upon request, Rael sent a forged [[Transponder code|transponder identification]]. While the identification was being scanned, Elk had the [[cruiser]] begin pulling in the [[V-21.1 Chevlex light haulcraft|Fondor Haulcraft]] by [[tractor beam]]. Rael's craft faked a burn in one of its [[Engine|thrusters]] to buy time while it simultaneously prepared countermeasures.<ref name="Daughter" />

Despite Rael's stalling, Elk made sure to prepare a boarding party for the Fondor [[Haulcraft]] while continuing to request its [[stabilizer]]s be powered down. Although the fake transponder ID gave a valid identification for the Imperials, the captain wished to still use the [[starship]] as practice and advised it to standby for boarding. In response, Rael engaged his thrusters, baiting Elk's cruiser into increasing its tractor forces. With that, the Fondor Haulcraft released shrapnel that was attracted to and tore apart the cruiser's forward tractor dish. Elk had the cruiser's [[Segra-Milo Imperial patrol's air wing|air wing]] pursue Rael's craft, but the enemy ship quickly destroyed the fighters and fled into [[hyperspace]].<ref name="Daughter" /> By [[3 BBY]], Gerrera and the Partisans were no longer headquartered on Segra Milo, instead operating from a [[Resistance base|base]] on<ref name="Ever Been">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}}</ref> the planet<ref name="D'Qar DB">{{Databank|d-qar|D'Qar}}</ref> [[D'Qar]].<ref name="Ever Been" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|A bit of a luxury I'd argue to a man who's hiding in cold caves and begging for spare parts.|Luthen Rael, to Saw Gerrera|<ref name="Narkina 5" />}}
Mines were established on Segra Milo and eventually exhausted. The Partisans used one as a launch base, having operations within a cavern whilst starfighters were parked outside.<ref name="Narkina 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
Segra Milo first appeared in "[[Narkina 5 (episode)|Narkina 5]],"<ref name="Narkina 5" /> the eighth episode of the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''. The episode was released on [[October 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="S1 Companion">{{InsiderCite|217|Star Wars: Andor Season One Companion|''Star Wars: Andor'' Season One Companion}}</ref> Scenes including Segra Milo were first seen before the episode's release in the official trailer for the season, which was published on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] channel on [[August 1]] of that year.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|cKOegEuCcfw|Andor &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+ (2:25)|sw_url=video/andor-official-trailer}}</ref> The caves on Segra Milo were filmed at the [[Wikipedia:Winspit|Winspit Quarry]], [[Wikipedia:Worth Matravers|Worth Matravers]] in [[Wikipedia:Dorset|Dorset]], [[Wikipedia:England|England]], a popular filming location that has been used in past live-action productions.<ref name="GBII">{{InsiderCite|219|Galactic Britain II: Cassian's Travels}}</ref>

